  "id": "broadband-noise",
  "term": "broadband noise",
  "definition": "Broadband noise is ambient noise spread across a wide range of frequencies that can mask other sounds, such as social calls. In this context, it reduces the acoustic information available to an animal and can change attention-related behaviour such as vigilance and foraging efficiency.",
